Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:36:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): skill_manage patch that changes nothing is a
 no_change success, not a batch-aborting error [daveey]

Agents send old_string == new_string on purpose to probe that a skill is
patchable (after a split or a patch-path fix), and re-send edits that already
landed. skill_manage rejected both with 'old_string and new_string are
identical', and since operations[] is the only call shape the error aborted
and rolled back every other op in the batch. The file patch tool already
treats these as no_change successes (is_already_applied); skill_manage never
got that path.

Now: identical strings present in the file, or new_string present with
old_string gone, return success + no_change + a note; the batch row carries
no_change/note; background-review summaries skip no_change rows so a no-op
is not announced as 'patched'. Identical strings absent from the file still
fail.
